              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#embedding_into_smooth_loci"} Embedding into smooth loci
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#SiteOfTowersOfCartesianSpaces"} The site of towers of Cartesian spaces and pro-morphisms
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em pro-manifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-object"} pro-object
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+limit"} projective limit
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
          %p
            Details depend on what exactly is understood by “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"}> manifold
            ”, i.e. whether
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
          %p
            Typically one wants to mean
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-objects"} pro-objects
            in manifolds of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+manifold"} infinite-dimensional manifold
            but with “mild” infinite dimensionality, expressed by the very fact that it may be presented as a formal projective limit of finite dimensional manifolds.
          %p
            To amplify this specification, one should properly speak of “pro-(finite dimensional smooth manifolds)”, but beware that people often abbreviate to “pro-manifold” regardless. Also “pro-finite manifold” is in use, which however, strictly speaking, is a misnomer since a “finite manifold” is one with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of points.
          %p
            An important example of pro-objects in finite-dimensional smooth manifolds are infinite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundles"} jet bundles
          %h2#procartesian_spaces Pro-Cartesian spaces
          %h3#embedding_into_smooth_loci Embedding into smooth loci
          #proCartSp.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
